    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nursĭa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nurtĭa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Sabine city</i>,
			the mod. <i>Norcia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frigida,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 715</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nursīnus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., Nursian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					10, 421</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 13, 34, § 130</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pilae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 20, 2</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nursīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Nursians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 12, 17, §
		107</span></i>.</div>
